# Milestone: M3 (semantics corrected at v1.0 / M10, design-risks v0.11.4-D)
# Covers: try/finally with no exception; finally ALWAYS runs, including on the
#         normal fall-through path — REVIVAL.md S5a: "finally runs on every exit
#         kind (return / throw / tag.stop / cancel) regardless."  The side
#         variable therefore reflects the finally body's assignment (99), not
#         the try body's (1).
# matrix-row: exceptions
#
# History: M3 emitted finally only on the unwind path; this fixture originally
# asserted `side == 1` (the pre-v1.0 bug).  v0.11.4-D fix (uemit_unwind.c,
# emit_finally_inline) runs the finally body on normal completion too.

var side = 0; try { side = 1 } finally { side = 99 }; side
[00000001] 99
